.PP
.B run_manual_sync
returns with
.B pending
set to true after the configured commands start in the background.  Poll
.B app_state.state.sync_in_progress
until it becomes false before checking the command result or refreshed mail
state.  The flag remains true until the post-sync search refresh also finishes.
Non-fixture harness checks may pass
.B test_refresh_delay_ms
(maximum 5000) to keep that refresh pending while testing responsiveness and
cancellation behavior.  Normal UI and command-palette syncs do not add this
delay.
.PP
.B compose_send
returns with
.B pending
set to true after the composed snapshot is queued.  Poll
.B app_state.state.send_in_progress
until it becomes false before checking
.BR last_send_report ,
.BR last_error ,
or send-related file changes.  If the primary window closes while a send is
pending, the application remains alive until send finalization completes.
.PP
.B close_main_window
closes only the primary window after returning its response.  Standalone
message windows are left open.
.PP
.B save_selected_attachment
and its
.B save_attachment
compatibility spelling open the normal GTK save chooser when the
.B dir
argument is omitted.  In fixture mode,
.B attachment_test_state
reports the pending chooser identifier, sanitized suggested name, visibility,
private Open directory, and fake-opener calls.  A test can then send:
.PP
.nf
{"command":"respond_attachment_save","args":{"id":1,"response":"accept","path":"/full/target"}}
.fi
.PP
or use
.B "response":"cancel".
Accept uses the complete target path and creates a numbered sibling rather than
replacing an existing file.  Cancel succeeds without writing or changing the
last operation, error, or status.  These two inspection/response commands are
rejected outside fixture mode.  Supplying an explicit
.B dir
to
.B save_selected_attachment
is a synchronous storage-test bypass and does not exercise the chooser.
.PP
Attachment Open writes a safely named file below an application-owned private
temporary directory before launching it.  The directory has mode 0700 on Unix
and is removed on normal process exit.  Fixture mode records the path in a fake
opener rather than starting an external application.
.PP
After
.BR open_settings ,
the fixture-only
.B settings_test_state
command reports the real dialog identifier and visible controls, the requested
theme and live resolved
.B theme_bg_color
and luminance with raw GTK properties, the configured preview limit, and the
actual rendered preview label's line limit, visibility, and text.
.B respond_settings
drives that same GTK dialog's response signal.  It accepts optional
.BR id ,
.BR theme ,
.BR thread_preview_lines ,
and
.B show_thread_preview
arguments and a
.B response
of
.BR apply ,
.BR save ,
or
.BR close .
For example:
.PP
.nf
{"command":"respond_settings","args":{"response":"apply","theme":"dark","thread_preview_lines":3,"show_thread_preview":true}}
.fi
.PP
Invalid theme or preview values leave the dialog open and change neither
runtime state nor the config file.
.B apply
changes the running window without writing;
.B save
writes and then applies.  These two inspection/response commands are rejected
outside fixture mode.  The older
.B save_settings
command persists only its basic direct-test fields and does not exercise the
dialog.
.SH SAFETY
Keep the socket local to the user session and use a token.  Prefer fixture data
for test-harness runs.  Fixture mode does not run configured receive,
database-update, or external-send commands; sends are captured locally and tag
changes are confined to the disposable fixture database.
.PP
On a non-fixture account,
.B automation.allow_live_send_test
must be true for
.B compose_send
and
.B automation.allow_live_tag_test
must be true for tag mutations.  Both default to false, and the gates also
apply when the operation is requested through
.BR run_command .
Non-fixture sync retains its separate explicit
.B [sync]
enablement.  Draft commands can change configured local files.  Attachment Save
uses the GTK chooser, while Attachment Open uses private temporary storage;
both are intentionally outside the send/tag gates.  The explicit attachment
.B dir
bypass writes to the requested directory and should be used only when that
local change is intended.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I artifacts/screenshots/
Default screenshot output directory for test-harness screenshots.
